  "content": {
    "id": "p40-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Cormac and Ciara agree to meet at a café sometime between 2 pm and 3 pm, but they have both forgotten the exact time. Each is equally likely to arrive at any time during that hour and will wait for at most 10 minutes for the other. Find the probability that they will meet.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{11}{36}$.\n\nUse the area where the arrival times differ by at most 10 minutes in a $60\\times60$ square.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ and $y$ be their arrival times in minutes after 2 pm. The pair $(x,y)$ is uniformly distributed in the square $0\\le x,y\\le60$. They meet when $|x-y|\\le10$.\n\nThe two excluded corner triangles each have perpendicular sides of length $50$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A_{\\text{meeting}}&=60^2-2\\left(\\frac12\\times50^2\\right)\\\\A_{\\text{meeting}}&=1100\\\\\\Pr(\\text{meeting})&=\\frac{1100}{3600}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{meeting})&=\\frac{11}{36}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 45
  },
